---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../../components/Crumbs.astro';
import ReviewNote from '../../components/ReviewNote.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Help shape Charitology and Charity OS" description="An invitation to charity leaders, founders and network organizers: share a practical problem, review a resource or explore a voluntary Charity OS pilot.">
  <header class="page-head"><div class="wrap"><Crumbs items={[{label:'For charities',href:'/for-charities/'},{label:'Help shape the work'}]} /><p class="eyebrow">An invitation to learn together</p><h1>What gets in<br />the way of the work?</h1><p class="lede">We want to hear from people running charities and the networks that support them. Help us build around a real problem, not an assumed one.</p><div class="invite-actions"><a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@charitology.org?subject=Charitology%20discovery%20conversation">Start a conversation</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href={url('/for-charities/networks/')}>Explore the networks</a></div></div></header>
  <div class="wrap invite-body">
    <div class="invite-grid">
      <section><p class="eyebrow">For charity teams</p><h2>Bring one difficult handover.</h2><p>Perhaps a donor update loses its owner, a grant deadline lives in someone’s inbox or a team cannot find the evidence behind a decision. We are proposing short discovery conversations about a specific piece of work.</p><p>You could describe the process in general terms, review a public resource or try a fictional example in the software. An initial conversation does not require an account, a migration or a commitment to use Charity OS.</p></section>
      <section><p class="eyebrow">For network organizers</p><h2>Help make the shared resources useful.</h2><p>Tell us whether a guide fits the people you support. Correct a listing, suggest a missing local organization or identify a question that deserves better shared guidance.</p><p>If a resource is useful, you decide whether it belongs in your community. We are not asking for a membership list or treating your network as an advertising channel.</p></section>
    </div>
    <section class="prose invite-section"><h2>A proposed first conversation</h2><ol><li><strong>The job.</strong> Walk through one recurring task and where a handover becomes difficult.</li><li><strong>The current method.</strong> Explain what already works and what must be preserved.</li><li><strong>The cost.</strong> Describe time, duplicated work and missing information without sharing sensitive records.</li><li><strong>The next test.</strong> Decide whether a guide, a small software example or no change would be useful.</li></ol><p>We suggest about twenty minutes as a starting point, with the format and timing agreed together. This is a proposed discovery process, not a completed study or evidence that our tools improve outcomes.</p></section>
    <section class="prose invite-section"><h2>What is available to explore</h2><ul><li><a href={url('/for-charities/fundraising/')}>Fundraising knowledge and practice:</a> method guides, a full-cost planner and follow-up schedules.</li><li><a href={url('/for-charities/networks/')}>Networks and founder programs:</a> selected official-source guides with access and scope limits.</li><li><a href="https://os.charitology.org">Shared Charity OS:</a> organization records, roles, linked tasks, review and recovery. Start with a fictional example.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/theguysaccount/charitology">The public repository:</a> inspect the code, suggest a correction or contribute through a pull request.</li></ul><p>The <a href={url('/for-charities/os-plan/')}>OS implementation plan</a> explains what is built and what remains. The software does not replace specialist accounting or case systems, and this invitation does not establish a funded program, professional accreditation or an institutional partnership.</p></section>
    <section class="prose invite-section"><h2>Choose what you share.</h2><p>Use an example without donor, staff or beneficiary records. Any interview notes should stay private to the agreed participants. Publication of an organization’s name, a quotation, a recording or a case study needs separate permission; a conversation alone supplies none.</p><p>For a private conversation, write to <a href="mailto:hello@charitology.org?subject=Charitology%20discovery%20conversation">hello@charitology.org</a> with your organization or network, the role you hold and the question you want to discuss. Please begin with a short description rather than attachments or personal case information. We will agree a next step together.</p><p>For a public directory suggestion, use the <a href="https://github.com/theguysaccount/charitology/issues/new?template=charity-network.yml">network suggestion form</a>. It asks for official organization sources. Opening it publishes nothing; submitting an issue makes its content public.</p></section>
    <ReviewNote filePath="src/pages/for-charities/collaborate.astro" title="Help shape Charitology" />
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  h1{max-width:17ch}.invite-actions{display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:1.5rem}.invite-body{padding-bottom:3rem}.invite-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:2rem;margin:1rem 0 3rem}.invite-grid>section{padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:var(--radius);background:var(--surface);min-width:0}.invite-grid h2{font-size:1.8rem}.invite-grid p{font-size:1rem}.invite-section{max-width:75ch;padding-block:2rem;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)}a{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:700px){.invite-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1rem}}
</style>
